import ZInQKernel.Compiler.NodeSkeleton.Main

/-!
# Kernel proof of the addition and multiplication counts of the halting circuit

`NodeCheck.haltingAddMulCheck : NodeCheck.HaltingAddMulCheck` (125,307 additions and 98,361
multiplications in the node list of the universal halting circuit) and the full
`NodeCheck.haltingNodeCheck : Universal.HaltingNodeCheck`, checked by the kernel.

* `Core.lean` (no Mathlib): a checking builder `HP` that transcribes the fast builder of
  `NodeCheck/` but keeps no hash-consing table; pinned oracle data says which calls hit (the
  hot list), which misses are local (checked against the recent records) and which are far
  (taken from sorted lanes).
* `Sim/`: `Sim2`, the simulation of the fast builder by the checking builder, for every
  primitive, macro and item, and the chaining lemmas (`cutS`).
* `Check.lean`, `Static.lean` (no Mathlib): the Boolean chunk check and the global checks of
  the hubs and lanes.
* `Data/` (generated by `gen/gen.py`, no Mathlib): the program, the oracle data, the pinned
  states and the 89 chunk theorems, each proved by `decide +kernel`.
* `Final.lean` (generated): the chain of chunks; `Main.lean`: the two theorems.
-/
